module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.service_interface_member_has_no_carrier

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data service_interface_member_has_no_carrier: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "service_interface_member_has_no_carrier" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a member of a v2 service declaration has no typed carrier, so the declaration-grade lowering (`v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_service_decl`) cannot lower it. The members fall into two classes, per DESIGN section 3 and docs/plans/service-interface-and-uses-carriers.md. INTERFACE facts: the operation modifiers `readonly` / `idempotent` / `hermetic` and an io field's `= default`. REALIZATION facts: `transport`, `config`, `exit`, `response`, `mock_response`, and an io field's `from \"key\"` wire key, which names the field of one transport's observation that fills a declared output and so is a decode projection of that transport, never part of the interface. Today's lowering sets the interface members aside as `body_lowering_reason_interface_member_unmodeled` and the realization members as `body_lowering_reason_realization_member_set_aside`, except that it still files the io `from` key under the interface reason because it reads the io tail as one unit; that misfiling is part of this class and moves with the realization binding.",
    "HARM: these are safety-relevant facts, not decoration. On the interface side, `idempotent` decides whether an automatic retry is admissible (DESIGN section 4b names a non-idempotent effect under retry as a class the ladder must reach), and a default decides what an omitted input becomes. On the realization side, a `from` key decides which wire field fills a declared output, and the transport, exit and response members decide how an observation becomes that output. A consumer that read the lowered service without them would retry what it must not, invent an omitted input, or read a field it was not given.",
    "CONTAINED, NOT SILENT: a set-aside member is unreachable as lowered, by construction. The lowering builds the set-aside population as a typed list (`ServiceSetAside`), and only census grade (`v2.compiler.normalize` `normalize_census`, whose carrier has no route past the symbol index) admits it as located advisories. Every other route refuses the service as `body_lowering_reason_service_realization_unreachable`, with each member's own located diagnostic pending, so no stage that would act on a service can assume a modifier's absence or a default transport.",
    "RELATED FRONTIER ON THE SAME LOWERING, RETIRED BY ITS TRIGGER (XL-2 service spine): a service's name used to lower as ONE label with the whole declared spelling (`shell.Find`), so a dotted reference to it did not resolve. Its trigger was v2 resolving service CALLS (D13 step b-pre), and the label migrated in one transition: a service now lowers as a spine, one segment per dotted part, every prefix a marked namespace body (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_service_node), and v2.compiler.namespace_graft namespace_graft_merge_namespace_bodies merges the bodies of services sharing a prefix (the sixteen shell.* services of dag/extdeps/shell.dag). An operation's declaration path is <module>.<service segments...>.<Op>. Only marked bodies merge, and a merged body grants no scope (v2.test.claim.normalize.service_spine).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigated (typed, located, counted set-aside; full normalize refuses). CEILING: structurally impossible -- every member is a field of a typed carrier, so a lowered service cannot exist without them. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: every member of every service in the corpus lowers into its carrier, which requires ALL of the following to exist: (1) for the effect claims `readonly` / `idempotent`, the Arrow effect-claims edge (`v2.std.node` `^arrow_effect_claims_edge`); (2) for `hermetic`, the separate Arrow execution-mode edge (`^arrow_execution_mode_claim_edge`); (3) for an io default, the one binder representation that carries an optional default, shared by fn parameters, io fields and record fields; and (4) for transport, config, exit, response, mock_response and the `from` wire key, a realization-binding sibling keyed by the operation's OperationRef. When all four exist, no ServiceSetAside has a producer and neither set-aside reason exists. Any subset is NOT sufficient: nearly every service-declaring module carries a realization member, and the interface carriers alone would unblock almost none of them (docs/plans/service-interface-and-uses-carriers.md; the population is re-measured on the CI census, not carried here).",
    "TRIGGER EXECUTED (gunbc#13833, merge 7c9319cbaf, measured_at 4ff78bc650). Executed at 4ff78bc650: full-door service-lowering admission; declared/undeclared argv-hole controls; declared/undeclared REST path-list-hole controls. No body-field-hole or method/verb/TLS/response-format value-validation guarantee is claimed. These executions remain off the required merge path (gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path). ServiceSetAside has no producer. RealizationMemberSetAside has no producer. A record-field `from` tail still produces interface_member_unmodeled -- that is a record-field residue, not a service member. gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status ServiceModuleLowering is PrerequisiteDelivered on this merge SHA.",
    "RELATED RESIDUE, UNVALIDATED REST `body` HOLE (filed so it is not lost): `extdeps.transports.rest_declared` `rest_binding_field_contract` maps RestBody (and method, query, headers, tls, auth_basic, response_format) to RestOtherContract, and `v2.compiler.service_realization` `realization_declared_field_refusal` returns optional_absent() for that arm -- no hole check. REST `path` is not this residue: it is RestStringTemplateContract. Path-segment holes go through `extdeps.uri_path` `parse_path_template`; `\{name\}` after `?` goes through `parse_query_template` (same `parse_segment_tokens`; unknown and unclosed refuse located; a name that appears twice is one input, RFC 6570 section 3.2.1). The REST lowering wall only binds those tokens. A body record of fields is not a URI template, so the two are not one mechanism. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a discriminating undeclared name in a REST `body` record refuses located on the same claim-run route as argv and path, and RestOtherContract is not an admit-any.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_declaration_lowering", decl_name: "census_counts_realization_and_unmodeled_interface_apart_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_declaration_lowering", decl_name: "full_door_admits_a_service_whose_members_lower_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "a_declared_input_hole_lowers_on_argv_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "an_undeclared_argv_hole_refuses_located_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "a_declared_input_hole_lowers_on_a_transport_list_field_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "an_undeclared_hole_in_a_transport_list_field_refuses_located_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_path_lowers_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_unknown_hole_refuses_located_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.normalize.service_realization_lowering", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_unclosed_brace_refuses_located_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.service_realization_conformance", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_path_binds_declared_holes_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.service_realization_conformance", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_unknown_hole_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.service_realization_conformance", decl_name: "a_rest_uri_template_unclosed_brace_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
